# Go
*.exe
*.test
*.out
/backup-manager
/dist/
/bin/

# SQLite journals produced by local runs
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Local config that may carry host keys or credentials
config.local.*
*.local.yaml

# Signing and key material. Release signatures are keyless (Sigstore), so
# a correct release never produces any of these; see
# docs/compliance/release-provenance.md. They are ignored anyway because
# the failure mode is permanent: a private key committed once stays in the
# history whatever is done to the working tree afterwards. Nothing tracked
# matches these patterns today, and scripts/release/publish-image.sh
# refuses to run at all beside a file that does, tracked or not, so this
# is the outer of two nets rather than the only one.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
cosign.key
cosign.pub

.DS_Store

# Agent worktrees, local only
.claude/

# A filled-in .env points at real key material on the host, and container/.env
# is what compose reads. The example stays tracked, the real one must not be.
.env
container/.env

# --- Frontend (ui/, apps/) -----------------------------------------------
# node_modules/ ignores the DIRECTORY. `**/node_modules/**` only ignores its
# CONTENTS, which leaves the directory entry itself untracked and not ignored,
# so `git clean -fd` and `git stash --include-untracked` delete the whole tree.
# Keep BOTH lines: the first protects the directory, the second still covers
# nested node_modules inside packages.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/**

# Vite/tsc build output. ui/shared/dist is what gets embedded into the Go
# binary at release time, so it is generated, never committed.
/ui/shared/dist/
# The per-provider bundle tree scripts/build-bundles.mjs writes (issue
# #180). Generated the same way dist/ is, one directory per provider, and
# consumed by a package's --ui-dir / --ui-root rather than committed.
/ui/shared/dist-bundles/
/ui/shared/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Playwright runtime artifacts. The specs under ui/shared/e2e/ are source and
# stay tracked; what a run writes is not.
/ui/shared/playwright-report/
/ui/shared/test-results/
/ui/shared/playwright/.cache/

# Coverage
/ui/shared/coverage/

# --- Python (scripts/deploy) ----------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# scripts/deploy/deploy_generic.py's own default --deploy-dir: rendered
# config.yaml/.env, which (per that script's own doc) point at real host
# key paths - generated locally, never committed, matching container/.env's
# own gitignore entry above.
/container/.generated/

# scripts/tests/ci-local-gate.test.sh sandbox: synthetic checkouts it builds,
# runs the gate against, and deletes again. Inside the repo rather than
# $TMPDIR so a test never creates or removes anything outside the checkout it
# belongs to.
/.ci-local-gate-test/

# scripts/perf/selftest.sh writes a deliberately-mutated baseline record here
# under a throwaway host id, to prove the performance gate refuses an
# incomplete record. It removes it again, but an interrupted run would leave
# it behind, and a mutated baseline is the last thing that should ever be
# committed by an absent-minded `git add -A`.
/docs/perf/baselines/selftest-tmp.json

# Where scripts/e2e/run-tests-repo-gate.sh builds the backup-manager it
# hands to the pinned CLI smoke slice. Inside the working tree on purpose:
# the alternative is a scratch directory under /tmp that the gate would then
# have to delete, and nothing this repository's tooling creates should need
# a recursive delete outside the workspace to clean up after itself.
/.e2e-gate/
/.e2e-two-machine/

# go.work.sum is a build product, regenerated by any `go` command that
# resolves the workspace, and this repository has never tracked it. It is
# ignored rather than merely absent because it kept coming back: three
# separate branches picked it up through `git add -A` after a build, and each
# time the three-layer boundary check caught it as a tracked file belonging to
# no layer (scripts/architecture/layers.conf classifies go.work and has no row
# for this). Ignoring it is what stops the next `git add -A` reintroducing it.
#
# go.work itself IS tracked and IS classified. The distinction is deliberate:
# the workspace definition is a decision somebody made, and its checksum file
# is a cache.
go.work.sum
